  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to happen to pass by",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to happen to pass by",
      "explanation": "To come by a place by chance, just when something is happening there."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "33679_toorikakaru_ex1",
      "japanese": "⟦{偶然|ぐうぜん}→偶然：02674_guuzen⟧⟦{友達|ともだち}→友達：01478_tomodachi⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{通|とお}りかかった。",
      "english": "A friend happened to pass by.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "33679_toorikakaru_ex2",
      "japanese": "⟦{店|みせ}→店：00497_mise⟧⟦の→の：09472_no⟧⟦{前|まえ}→前：02255_mae⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{通|とお}りかかった。",
      "english": "I happened to walk past the shop.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "33679_toorikakaru_ex3",
      "japanese": "⟦{困|こま}っていた→困る：00861_komaru⟧⟦ところ→ところ：01137_tokoro⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧⟦{親切|しんせつ}→親切：01144_shinsetsu⟧な⟦{人|ひと}→人：00476_hito⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{通|とお}りかかって、⟦{道|みち}→道：00505_michi⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{教|おし}えて→教える：00526_oshieru⟧⟦くれた→くれる：00724_kureru⟧。",
      "english": "Just when I was stuck, a kind person happened along and showed me the way.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "⟦{通|とお}る→通る：01243_tooru⟧ (to pass) + ⟦かかる→かかる：00711_kakaru⟧ (to come upon). The point is chance timing: the person was not coming on purpose. Also written {通|とお}り{掛|か}かる.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦{偶然|ぐうぜん}→偶然：02674_guuzen⟧{通|とお}りかかる: to chance to pass by\n- 〜⟦の→の：09472_no⟧⟦{前|まえ}→前：02255_mae⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{通|とお}りかかる: to happen to pass in front of\n- {通|とお}りかかった⟦{人|ひと}→人：00476_hito⟧: a passer-by\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{通|とお}り{過|す}ぎる→通り過ぎる：02372_toorisugiru⟧: to go past without stopping; no idea of chance",
